sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Data Scientist
    participant KubeAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Webhook as Validating Webhook<br/>9443/TCP TLS
    participant Reconciler as Framework Reconciler<br/>(PyTorch/TF/MPI/JAX/XGBoost/Paddle)
    participant Workers as Worker Pods
    participant Prometheus as Prometheus<br/>8080/TCP HTTP
    participant OpenShift as OpenShift APIServer<br/>config.openshift.io/v1

    Note over Webhook,OpenShift: Startup: TLS Configuration Flow
    Reconciler->>KubeAPI: GET config.openshift.io/v1/APIServer "cluster"
    KubeAPI-->>Reconciler: TLS profile (cipher suites, min version)
    alt OpenShift cluster
        Reconciler->>Reconciler: Apply cluster TLS profile to webhook server
    else Non-OpenShift / unavailable
        Reconciler->>Reconciler: Apply intermediate profile<br/>TLS 1.2 min, 6 AEAD ciphers
    end

    Note over User,Prometheus: Job Submission Flow
    User->>KubeAPI: kubectl apply -f pytorchjob.yaml<br/>(CREATE PyTorchJob CR)
    KubeAPI->>Webhook: POST /validate-kubeflow-org-v1-pytorchjob<br/>Port 443 → 9443, TLS
    alt Valid job spec
        Webhook-->>KubeAPI: Allowed
        KubeAPI-->>User: pytorchjob.kubeflow.org/my-job created
    else Invalid job spec
        Webhook-->>KubeAPI: Denied (Fail policy)
        KubeAPI-->>User: Error: admission webhook rejected
    end

    Note over Reconciler,Workers: Reconciliation Loop
    KubeAPI->>Reconciler: Watch event: PyTorchJob created
    Reconciler->>KubeAPI: Create worker Pods
    Reconciler->>KubeAPI: Create worker Services
    Reconciler->>KubeAPI: Create NetworkPolicy (workload isolation)
    opt PyTorch elastic training
        Reconciler->>KubeAPI: Create HorizontalPodAutoscaler
    end
    opt MPI framework
        Reconciler->>KubeAPI: Create ConfigMap, ServiceAccount,<br/>Role, RoleBinding
    end
    opt Gang scheduling enabled
        Reconciler->>KubeAPI: Create PodGroup<br/>(Volcano or scheduler-plugins)
    end
    KubeAPI-->>Workers: Pods scheduled and running

    loop Training in progress
        Reconciler->>KubeAPI: Watch Pod status changes
        KubeAPI-->>Reconciler: Pod phase updates
        Reconciler->>KubeAPI: PATCH PyTorchJob/status<br/>(replica counts, conditions)
    end

    Workers-->>KubeAPI: Training complete (Pod succeeded)
    Reconciler->>KubeAPI: Update PyTorchJob status: Succeeded
    Reconciler->>KubeAPI: Cleanup resources

    Note over Prometheus,Reconciler: Observability
    Prometheus->>Reconciler: GET /metrics<br/>Port 8080, HTTP
    Reconciler-->>Prometheus: Prometheus metrics
